{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 109, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the direct input-output residual helps most when no 0->3 path existed before."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the skip residual on edge 3 hurts more than removing a conv there, since the residual is critical for trainability."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Cutting node 1 when node 2 is fed only by pooling leaves almost no learnable path, causing catastrophic drops."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the 0->3 shortcut, removing edge 0 strips much more of the cell's remaining signal paths."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Activating a dead edge into the output adds a whole computational path, whereas replacing an existing op yields smaller or negative changes."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When node 1 receives no input, edge 4 carries zeros, so changing its op is nearly neutral compared with its positive effect otherwise."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on a missing edge adds capacity, while replacing a skip removes a useful shortcut."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 5 supplies a residual-like path to the output when edge 3 lacks one, but is redundant and capacity-reducing when edge 3 is already a skip."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "directi